<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War in Afghanistan (2001–2021)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2001–2021</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> was fought from 2001 to 2021 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and its allies invaded Afghanistan following the attacks of 11 September 2001 and overthrew the Taliban government that sheltered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda">al-Qaeda</a>. A long insurgency followed against the new Afghan state and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> forces; after the United States agreed to withdraw, the Taliban took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in August 2021 and restored their regime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-in-afghanistan-2001-2021.jpg" alt="War in Afghanistan (2001–2021)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pfc. Cameron Boyd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:U.S._Army_firefight_in_Kunar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
